    {
      "text": "When Herod … heard these things, he was troubled, Matt. 2:3. wars and rumours of wars: … be not troubled, Matt. 24:6 (Mark 13:7; JS—M 1:23). they all saw him, and were troubled, Mark 6:50. shall be famines and troubles, Mark 13:8. he said unto them, Why are ye troubled, Luke 24:38. angel … troubled the water, John 5:4. When Jesus had thus said, he was troubled in spirit, John 13:21. Let not your heart be troubled, John 14:1 (14:27; D&C 98:18). my sentence is, that we trouble not them, Acts 15:19. comfort them which are in any trouble, 2 Cor. 1:4. We are troubled on every side, 2 Cor. 4:8. there be some that trouble you, Gal. 1:7. he that troubleth you shall bear his judgment, Gal. 5:10. lest any root of bitterness … trouble you, Heb. 12:15. be not afraid of their terror, neither be troubled, 1 Pet. 3:14.",
